test/healthz.test.js with node:test and assert, minimal req/res stubs. Must cover healthz triple, 404, 500. For 500, how to trigger? "处理中同步异常（try/catch）" — need injection mechanism. Design says "请求处理被注入一次抛出 Error 的调用". How does the test inject? Perhaps handleRequest has a route hook, or we can pass a req whose property getter throws. E.g. make `req.url` getter throw → handleRequest's try/catch catches → 500. That's elegant: in-process injection without extra API.

Let me design app.js:

```js
"use strict";

const JSON_CONTENT_TYPE = "application/json; charset=utf-8";

function sendJson(res, statusCode, payload) {
  if (res.headersSent || res.writableEnded) return;
  const body = JSON.stringify(payload);
  res.statusCode = statusCode;
  res.setHeader("content-type", JSON_CONTENT_TYPE);
  res.end(body);
}

function handleRequest(req, res) {
  try {
    const method = req.method;
    const url = req.url || "/";
    const pathname = url.split("?")[0];
    if (method === "GET" && pathname === "/healthz") {
      sendJson(res, 200, { status: "ok" });
      return;
    }
    sendJson(res, 404, { error: "not_found" });
  } catch (error) {
    process.stderr.write(`request failed: ${error && error.message}\n`);
    if (!res.headersSent && !res.writableEnded) {
      sendJson(res, 500, { error: "internal_error" });
    }
  }
}

module.exports = { handleRequest, createHandler };
```

Wait: if error thrown by req.url getter, then in catch sendJson uses res — fine. But careful: if exception thrown after headers sent, can't respond; then the test wouldn't get 500. Our test will throw before headers.

Also, sending 500 through sendJson inside catch: sendJson itself could throw if res is broken; wrap? Keep simple.

